          "filename": "Birmingham City Council House - geograph.org.uk - 1309269.jpg",
          "caption": "Birmingham City Council House It is located in Victoria Square in the city centre and is a Grade II* listed building. Above the main entrance, which faces Victoria Square, is a mosaic by Salviati Burke and Co. of Venice. Above that, the pediment shows Britannia receiving the manufacturers of Birmingham. The carved decoration on the entablature includes green men.",
